// The per-behaviour state-release proof over a function's SIR (chunk15_stack_memory_design.md §4.1,
// decision 18; chunk 15 phase 3c, 2026-10-30). Shared by the emitters (the proof goes into the
// behaviour's prefix word and its epilogue flag) and by main_compile_pipeline (W2300 for an unproven
// behaviour, §4.5).
//
// A behaviour is a function returning (:reply, R, S) or (:no_reply, S); its state parameter is the
// second one. A slot is a node-bearing position of S (§4.1), so a behaviour whose S carries no pointer
// (int64, atom, an atom-only sum, actor_ref, ...) has no slot and is proven as it stands: the runtime
// answers a scalar state as given (prims_actors_state_asm@_silica_rt_state_dispatch_end), and the
// counter's `(:reply, state, state + 1)` must not pay a whole-state copy or print W2300 (found by the
// 3c gate: 332 of actors_addition's 359 W2300 were "built by 'add'" on an int64 state). S is read from
// the return type (sr_state_type), not from param_types, whose `|` separator is also the sum spelling.
// OLD names denote the old state or a part of it reached only through projections: the
// parameter, every let whose value is an Old name or a record_proj / tuple_proj chain over one, and
// every `bind` arm over such a scrutinee. The Old set is a set of names, so a name is trusted only while
// its binding is in scope: a let (or bind arm) that rebinds a name to a value that is not Old removes
// the name for the walk of its body and marks it (`~name`), and a marked name is dropped from the set
// once the walk is over. Every tuple decomposition names its root `%_td_0` (tuple_decompose), so a
// behaviour that decomposes both its state and its message binds `%_td_0` twice; without the scoping a
// part of the message projected from the second `%_td_0` passed as a part of the old state (found
// 2026-11-06: actors_addition/failure_reports_kept_and_forwarded's logger kept every report string in
// its state chain and exhausted the board heap). For the same reason a reference to a let-bound name is
// resolved to the innermost let of that name whose body holds the reference (sr_find_let_value_at), not
// to the first let of the name. The proof holds when, in every arm of the body, the new state
// (the third element of the result tuple, the second for :no_reply) is
//   * an Old name or a projection of one (the whole state, or a part of it, passed through), or
//   * a record_make / tuple_make whose pointer-carrying operands are each a projection of an Old name
//     (a nested record_make / tuple_make is a by-value aggregate and is checked the same way) and no
//     two of them are the same projection (P2: one version reaches one slot).
// Everything else is unproven, with the reason the design names: a pointer-carrying operand that is a
// user call ("'f' is not a logging updater": no logging updater exists before the stdlib's phase 5, so
// every update is unproven, which is the conservative side of P4), any other fresh value ("slot 'q' is
// replaced without an update": its old nodes could never be released, §4.1 "what release does not
// cover"; a projection of a value that is not Old, a part of the message, says "by a part of '%msg'"),
// the same projection kept twice, a record / tuple / list pattern over the old state ("hides
// its parts", as mc_case_arms_step poisons with "!"), a result that is a call or a shape not analysed.
// A write_ref anywhere in the body is unproven too: a frame value written into an old state cell is
// not reached by the evacuation (§4.3 step 1 leaves old nodes alone); §6.3's E2302 takes this over in
// phase 6. The `|_upd=` update-call rules of §4.1 are not needed until a logging updater exists.
// Buffers in state (Lee 2026-11-01, design §4.2): when S is one of the buffer shapes of
// state_buffer_variant, a buffer-valued operand of the new state is accepted whatever it is, and an atom
// literal new state is accepted when nothing but buffers and the root shell can be dropped by it; the
// behaviour's epilogue (prims_actors@bmv_state_buffer_retire_asm) retires each old buffer that is not one
// of the new state's buffer words, so a replaced buffer is freed on the proven path.
//
// SIR shapes read here (sir_generator/terms): a user call is kind 4 / 5 with `inner` the first argument
// and `right_expr` a `user_call_rest` chain; tuple_make(inner = e1, right = e2 | tuple_make(...));
// record_make(name = field, inner = value, right = the next field or nothing); record_proj(name =
// field, inner = the record); tuple_proj(inner = the tuple, right = the index constant); a kind-8 arm
// has `value` "bind" / "record" / "tuple" / "list_cons" and `name` its binding. The node list is stored
// newest first (sir_return_position@rp_node_at).

export behaviour_release_reason/1;
export is_behaviour_return_type/1;
export behaviour_pin_error/1;
export state_buffer_variant/1;
export state_buffer_field_names/1;

fn sr_nodes_len(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)]) -> int64 {
    sequence proc[mem(normal)]
        result: int64 <- length[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)](nodes)
    produces
        pure result
    end
}

fn sr_node_at(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64) -> { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> { kind: -1, type_name: "", value: "", name: "", inner: -1, right_expr: -1 };
        false -> {
            n: int64 <- sr_nodes_len(nodes);
            case idx >= n of {
                true -> { kind: -1, type_name: "", value: "", name: "", inner: -1, right_expr: -1 };
                false -> {
                    e: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- list_nth(nodes, n - 1 - idx);
                    { kind: e.kind, type_name: e.type_name, value: e.value, name: e.name, inner: e.inner, right_expr: e.right_expr }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ---- strings and sets (",a,b,") -----------------------------------------------------------------

fn sr_strip_spaces(s: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(s) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> case substring(s, 0, 1) == " " of {
            true -> sr_strip_spaces(substring(s, 1, length_bytes(s)));
            false -> concat(substring(s, 0, 1), sr_strip_spaces(substring(s, 1, length_bytes(s))))
        }
    }
}

fn sr_starts_with(s: string, p: string) -> boolean {
    length_bytes(s) >= length_bytes(p) and substring(s, 0, length_bytes(p)) == p
}

fn sr_find_from(s: string, needle: string, i: int64) -> int64 {
    case i + length_bytes(needle) > length_bytes(s) of {
        true -> -1;
        false -> case substring(s, i, i + length_bytes(needle)) == needle of {
            true -> i;
            false -> sr_find_from(s, needle, i + 1)
        }
    }
}

fn sr_in_set(set: string, name: string) -> boolean {
    length_bytes(name) > 0 and sr_find_from(set, concat(",", concat(name, ",")), 0) >= 0
}

fn sr_add(set: string, name: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(name) == 0 or sr_in_set(set, name) of {
        true -> set;
        false -> case length_bytes(set) == 0 of {
            true -> concat(",", concat(name, ","));
            false -> concat(set, concat(name, ","))
        }
    }
}

// A name and its parameter spelling (`%name`): the SIR refers to a parameter with the prefix.
fn sr_add_both(set: string, name: string) -> string {
    case sr_starts_with(name, "%") of {
        true -> sr_add(sr_add(set, name), substring(name, 1, length_bytes(name)));
        false -> sr_add(sr_add(set, name), concat("%", name))
    }
}

// The set without name (",a,b," without "b" is ",a,"); a name that is not in it leaves it as it is.
fn sr_remove(set: string, name: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(name) == 0 of {
        true -> set;
        false -> {
            p: int64 <- sr_find_from(set, concat(",", concat(name, ",")), 0);
            case p < 0 of {
                true -> set;
                false -> concat(substring(set, 0, p), substring(set, p + length_bytes(name) + 1, length_bytes(set)))
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_remove_both(set: string, name: string) -> string {
    case sr_starts_with(name, "%") of {
        true -> sr_remove(sr_remove(set, name), substring(name, 1, length_bytes(name)));
        false -> sr_remove(sr_remove(set, name), concat("%", name))
    }
}

// A name rebound to a value that is not Old: out of the set for the walk of the binding's body, and
// marked (`~name`, both spellings) so that sr_strip_marked drops it once the walk is over, since the
// name alone no longer says which binding a reference means. No SIR name starts with '~'.
fn sr_mark_rebound(set: string, name: string) -> string {
    bare: string <- sr_strip_pct(name);
    case length_bytes(bare) == 0 of {
        true -> set;
        false -> sr_add(sr_add(sr_remove_both(set, name), concat("~", bare)), concat("~%", bare))
    }
}

// The entries of set from the comma at pos, without the marks and without every name that carries one.
fn sr_strip_marked(set: string, pos: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case pos + 1 >= length_bytes(set) of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            e: int64 <- sr_find_from(set, ",", pos + 1);
            case e < 0 of {
                true -> acc;
                false -> {
                    entry: string <- substring(set, pos + 1, e);
                    mark: string <- concat("~", entry);
                    acc1: string <- case sr_starts_with(entry, "~") or sr_in_set(set, mark) of {
                        true -> acc;
                        false -> sr_add(acc, entry)
                    };
                    sr_strip_marked(set, e, acc1)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The idx-th name of "a|b|c".
fn sr_param_at(names: string, idx: int64) -> string {
    case length_bytes(names) == 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            p: int64 <- sr_find_from(names, "|", 0);
            case p < 0 of {
                true -> case idx == 0 of { true -> names; false -> "" };
                false -> case idx == 0 of {
                    true -> substring(names, 0, p);
                    false -> sr_param_at(substring(names, p + 1, length_bytes(names)), idx - 1)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ---- types -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn is_behaviour_return_type(return_type: string) -> boolean {
    t: string <- sr_strip_spaces(return_type);
    sr_starts_with(t, "(:reply,") or sr_starts_with(t, "(:no_reply,")
}

// The state type S of a (space-stripped) behaviour return type `(:reply,R,S)` / `(:no_reply,S)`: the text
// after the last comma at depth 1, without the closing parenthesis. A comma inside (), [] or {} belongs
// to R or S (a record state, `List[T,mem(normal)]`, a tuple variant of a sum). "" when rt is no tuple.
fn sr_state_type_scan(rt: string, i: int64, depth: int64, last: int64) -> string {
    case i >= length_bytes(rt) - 1 of {
        true -> substring(rt, last + 1, length_bytes(rt) - 1);
        false -> {
            c: string <- substring(rt, i, i + 1);
            case c == "(" or c == "[" or c == "{" of {
                true -> sr_state_type_scan(rt, i + 1, depth + 1, last);
                false -> case c == ")" or c == "]" or c == "}" of {
                    true -> sr_state_type_scan(rt, i + 1, depth - 1, last);
                    false -> case c == "," and depth == 1 of {
                        true -> sr_state_type_scan(rt, i + 1, depth, i);
                        false -> sr_state_type_scan(rt, i + 1, depth, last)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_state_type(rt: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(rt) >= 2 and sr_starts_with(rt, "(") of {
        true -> sr_state_type_scan(rt, 0, 0, 0);
        false -> ""
    }
}

// Every top-level alternative of a (space-stripped) sum is an atom literal (`:on|:off`): no pointer. An
// alternative that is not an atom (a record, a tuple, a list, a named type) answers false.
fn sr_atoms_only(t: string) -> boolean {
    case length_bytes(t) == 0 of {
        true -> true;
        false -> case sr_starts_with(t, ":") of {
            false -> false;
            true -> {
                bar: int64 <- sr_find_from(t, "|", 0);
                alt: string <- case bar < 0 of { true -> t; false -> substring(t, 0, bar) };
                case sr_find_from(alt, "(", 0) >= 0 or sr_find_from(alt, "[", 0) >= 0 or sr_find_from(alt, "{", 0) >= 0 or sr_find_from(alt, ",", 0) >= 0 of {
                    true -> false;
                    false -> case bar < 0 of {
                        true -> true;
                        false -> sr_atoms_only(substring(t, bar + 1, length_bytes(t)))
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// A type that may hold a pointer (sir_return_position@rp_type_may_point, with the atom sums and the
// one-word runtime handles of the evacuation's word kinds added). An unknown type may.
fn sr_type_may_point(t0: string) -> boolean {
    t: string <- sr_strip_spaces(t0);
    case t of {
        "int64" -> false;
        "uint64" -> false;
        "int32" -> false;
        "uint32" -> false;
        "int16" -> false;
        "uint16" -> false;
        "int8" -> false;
        "uint8" -> false;
        "float64" -> false;
        "float32" -> false;
        "float16" -> false;
        "boolean" -> false;
        "bool" -> false;
        "char" -> false;
        "atom" -> false;
        "unit" -> false;
        "actor_ref" -> false;
        "timer_ref" -> false;
        "state_policy" -> false;
        "stack_policy" -> false;
        "lifetime" -> false;
        _: string -> case sr_starts_with(t, ":") of {
            true -> sr_atoms_only(t) == false;
            false -> true
        }
    }
}

// ---- buffers in state (Lee 2026-11-01; design §4.2) ---------------------------------------------
//
// A state shape whose buffers sit only where the behaviour epilogue can compare them word for word
// (prims_actors@bmv_state_buffer_retire_asm): S is a buffer, a record whose every field is a buffer or a
// type with no buffer anywhere in it, or a sum of atom literals and exactly one such buffer or record.
// In such an S a buffer value can only be stored in one of those buffer positions (the type rules), so an
// old buffer is reachable from the new state iff it is one of the new state's buffer words; the
// epilogue retires every other old buffer and the dispatch end frees it after the evacuation.

// The first `ch` at bracket depth 0 of s at or after i, or -1.
fn sr_top_find(s: string, ch: string, i: int64, depth: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= length_bytes(s) of {
        true -> -1;
        false -> {
            c: string <- substring(s, i, i + 1);
            case depth == 0 and c == ch of {
                true -> i;
                false -> case c == "(" or c == "[" or c == "{" of {
                    true -> sr_top_find(s, ch, i + 1, depth + 1);
                    false -> case c == ")" or c == "]" or c == "}" of {
                        true -> sr_top_find(s, ch, i + 1, depth - 1);
                        false -> sr_top_find(s, ch, i + 1, depth)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_is_atom_alt(alt: string) -> boolean {
    sr_starts_with(alt, ":") and sr_find_from(alt, "(", 0) < 0 and sr_find_from(alt, "[", 0) < 0 and sr_find_from(alt, "{", 0) < 0 and sr_find_from(alt, ",", 0) < 0
}

// The one alternative of a (space-stripped) sum that is not an atom literal: "" when there is none,
// "?" when there are two or more.
fn sr_nonatom_alt(s: string, acc: string) -> string {
    bar: int64 <- sr_top_find(s, "|", 0, 0);
    alt: string <- case bar < 0 of { true -> s; false -> substring(s, 0, bar) };
    acc1: string <- case sr_is_atom_alt(alt) of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> case length_bytes(acc) == 0 of { true -> alt; false -> "?" }
    };
    case bar < 0 of {
        true -> acc1;
        false -> sr_nonatom_alt(substring(s, bar + 1, length_bytes(s)), acc1)
    }
}

fn sr_is_buf_type(t: string) -> boolean {
    sr_starts_with(sr_strip_spaces(t), "buf(")
}

// The record body's fields from i: the number that are buffers, or -1 when a field holds a buffer
// inside another type (a List of buffers, a ref to one, a nested record with one).
fn sr_record_buf_count(body: string, i: int64, acc: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= length_bytes(body) of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            comma: int64 <- sr_top_find(body, ",", i, 0);
            seg_end: int64 <- case comma < 0 of { true -> length_bytes(body); false -> comma };
            seg: string <- substring(body, i, seg_end);
            colon: int64 <- sr_find_from(seg, ":", 0);
            fty: string <- case colon < 0 of { true -> seg; false -> substring(seg, colon + 1, length_bytes(seg)) };
            acc1: int64 <- case sr_is_buf_type(fty) of {
                true -> acc + 1;
                false -> case sr_find_from(fty, "buf(", 0) >= 0 of { true -> -1; false -> acc }
            };
            case acc1 < 0 of {
                true -> -1;
                false -> sr_record_buf_count(body, seg_end + 1, acc1)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The names of the record body's buffer fields from i, each followed by a comma ("b,c,").
fn sr_record_buf_names(body: string, i: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case i >= length_bytes(body) of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            comma: int64 <- sr_top_find(body, ",", i, 0);
            seg_end: int64 <- case comma < 0 of { true -> length_bytes(body); false -> comma };
            seg: string <- substring(body, i, seg_end);
            colon: int64 <- sr_find_from(seg, ":", 0);
            acc1: string <- case colon > 0 and sr_is_buf_type(substring(seg, colon + 1, length_bytes(seg))) of {
                true -> concat(acc, concat(substring(seg, 0, colon), ","));
                false -> acc
            };
            sr_record_buf_names(body, seg_end + 1, acc1)
        }
    }
}

// The buffer field names of a state_buffer_variant record ("b,c,"); "" for a buffer variant.
fn state_buffer_field_names(variant: string) -> string {
    sr_record_buf_names(sr_record_body(sr_strip_spaces(variant)), 0, "")
}

// Every field of the record body from i that is not a buffer is pointer-free.
fn sr_record_rest_scalar(body: string, i: int64) -> boolean {
    case i >= length_bytes(body) of {
        true -> true;
        false -> {
            comma: int64 <- sr_top_find(body, ",", i, 0);
            seg_end: int64 <- case comma < 0 of { true -> length_bytes(body); false -> comma };
            seg: string <- substring(body, i, seg_end);
            colon: int64 <- sr_find_from(seg, ":", 0);
            fty: string <- case colon < 0 of { true -> seg; false -> substring(seg, colon + 1, length_bytes(seg)) };
            case sr_is_buf_type(fty) or sr_type_may_point(fty) == false of {
                true -> sr_record_rest_scalar(body, seg_end + 1);
                false -> false
            }
        }
    }
}

// A sum written in parentheses, `(:none|{...})`, without them; anything else (a tuple included) as given.
fn sr_unparen_sum(s: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(s) >= 2 and sr_starts_with(s, "(") and sr_top_find(s, ")", 1, 0) == length_bytes(s) - 1 of {
        false -> s;
        true -> {
            inner: string <- substring(s, 1, length_bytes(s) - 1);
            case sr_top_find(inner, "|", 0, 0) >= 0 and sr_top_find(inner, ",", 0, 0) < 0 of {
                true -> inner;
                false -> s
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_record_body(t: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(t) >= 2 and sr_starts_with(t, "{") and substring(t, length_bytes(t) - 1, length_bytes(t)) == "}" of {
        true -> substring(t, 1, length_bytes(t) - 1);
        false -> ""
    }
}

// The buffer-bearing part of a behaviour's state type: the buffer type itself, or the record type
// (space-stripped) whose buffer fields the epilogue compares; "" when S is not such a shape (no buffer,
// or a buffer the epilogue cannot reach by one field offset: those stay live, the conservative choice).
// The tuple buffer shape (sr_region_buffer_tuple) answers "#tuplebuf," followed by its buffer type: the
// epilogue retire then compares element 1 of the old and new root tuples (prims_actors@bmv_state_buffer_retire_asm).
fn state_buffer_variant(return_type: string) -> string {
    tb: string <- sr_region_buffer_tuple_buf(return_type);
    case length_bytes(tb) > 0 of {
        true -> concat("#tuplebuf,", tb);
        false -> sr_state_buffer_variant_plain(return_type)
    }
}

fn sr_state_buffer_variant_plain(return_type: string) -> string {
    s: string <- sr_unparen_sum(sr_state_type(sr_strip_spaces(return_type)));
    alt: string <- sr_nonatom_alt(s, "");
    case length_bytes(alt) == 0 or alt == "?" of {
        true -> "";
        false -> case sr_is_buf_type(alt) of {
            true -> alt;
            false -> {
                body: string <- sr_record_body(alt);
                case length_bytes(body) > 0 and sr_record_buf_count(body, 0, 0) > 0 of {
                    true -> alt;
                    false -> ""
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The tuple buffer shape (Lee 2026-11-01: a buffer in actor state comes with its region): S is exactly
// `(region(L, m), A)` with A a sum of atom literals and one buffer. The region member is carried: being
// pointer-carrying, the proof accepts it only as an Old projection (the old state's region; a fresh
// region is "replaced without an update"). The buffer member is accepted as a buffer at the root is
// ("#bufstate"). state_buffer_variant answers "#tuplebuf,<buf type>" for it, and the epilogue retire
// (prims_actors@bmv_state_buffer_retire_asm, tuple branch) compares element 1 (offset 8; a tuple has no
// shape word) of the old and new root tuples.
fn sr_region_buffer_tuple(return_type: string) -> boolean {
    length_bytes(sr_region_buffer_tuple_buf(return_type)) > 0
}

// The buffer type of the tuple buffer shape; "" when S is not that shape.
fn sr_region_buffer_tuple_buf(return_type: string) -> string {
    s: string <- sr_state_type(sr_strip_spaces(return_type));
    n: int64 <- length_bytes(s);
    case n >= 2 and sr_starts_with(s, "(") and sr_top_find(s, ")", 1, 0) == n - 1 of {
        false -> "";
        true -> {
            inner: string <- substring(s, 1, n - 1);
            c: int64 <- sr_top_find(inner, ",", 0, 0);
            case c > 0 and sr_top_find(inner, ",", c + 1, 0) < 0 of {
                false -> "";
                true -> {
                    m1: string <- sr_unparen_sum(substring(inner, c + 1, length_bytes(inner)));
                    alt: string <- sr_nonatom_alt(m1, "");
                    case sr_starts_with(substring(inner, 0, c), "region(") and sr_top_find(m1, "|", 0, 0) >= 0 and sr_is_buf_type(alt) of {
                        true -> alt;
                        false -> ""
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The state may become an atom literal and lose nothing but buffers and the root shell: S has an atom
// alternative and its buffer part is a buffer or a record whose other fields are pointer-free.
fn sr_literal_state_ok(return_type: string, variant: string) -> boolean {
    s: string <- sr_unparen_sum(sr_state_type(sr_strip_spaces(return_type)));
    sr_top_find(s, "|", 0, 0) >= 0 and (sr_is_buf_type(variant) or sr_record_rest_scalar(sr_record_body(variant), 0))
}

// Under a buffer shape (the "#bufstate" marker in the Old set) a buffer-valued operand of the new state
// is accepted whatever it is: a fresh alloc_buf / alloc_buf_retained, a buffer a call returned, or an
// old buffer moved to another field. The epilogue keeps every old buffer that is one of the new state's
// buffer words and retires the others, so no alias of an old buffer can be freed. Under "#litstate" an
// atom literal new state is accepted: it reaches nothing.
fn sr_buffer_operand_ok(n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, old: string) -> boolean {
    case sr_in_set(old, "#bufstate") of {
        false -> false;
        true -> sr_is_buf_type(n.type_name) or (n.kind == 6 and (n.name == "alloc_buf" or n.name == "alloc_buf_retained"))
    }
}

fn sr_literal_operand_ok(n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, old: string) -> boolean {
    sr_in_set(old, "#litstate") and n.kind == 0 and (sr_starts_with(n.value, ":") or sr_type_may_point(n.type_name) == false)
}

// ---- the Old set: the state and its projections --------------------------------------------------

// The node is an Old name or a record_proj / tuple_proj chain over one.
fn sr_is_old_proj(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string) -> boolean {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> false;
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind == 1 of {
                true -> sr_in_set(old, a.name);
                false -> case a.kind == 6 and (a.name == "record_proj" or a.name == "tuple_proj") of {
                    true -> sr_is_old_proj(nodes, a.inner, old);
                    false -> false
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_old_step(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> old;
        false -> {
            n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            old1: string <- case n.kind == 2 of {
                false -> old;
                true -> case sr_is_old_proj(nodes, n.inner, old) of {
                    true -> sr_add_both(old, n.name);
                    false -> sr_mark_rebound(old, n.name)
                }
            };
            old2: string <- case n.kind == 3 of {
                true -> sr_old_arms(nodes, n.right_expr, sr_is_old_proj(nodes, n.inner, old1), old1);
                false -> old1
            };
            old3: string <- sr_old_step(nodes, n.inner, old2);
            case n.kind == 3 of {
                true -> old3;
                false -> sr_old_step(nodes, n.right_expr, old3)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_old_arms(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, scrut_old: boolean, old: string) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> old;
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind == 7 of {
                true -> sr_old_arms(nodes, a.right_expr, scrut_old, sr_old_arms(nodes, a.inner, scrut_old, old));
                false -> case a.kind == 8 of {
                    false -> sr_old_step(nodes, idx, old);
                    true -> {
                        old1: string <- case scrut_old and a.value == "bind" of {
                            true -> sr_add_both(old, a.name);
                            false -> case scrut_old and (a.value == "record" or a.value == "tuple" or a.value == "list_cons") of {
                                true -> sr_add(old, "!");
                                false -> case a.value == "bind" of {
                                    true -> sr_mark_rebound(old, a.name);
                                    false -> old
                                }
                            }
                        };
                        sr_old_step(nodes, a.right_expr, sr_old_step(nodes, a.inner, old1))
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_old_closure(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], root: int64, old: string, rounds: int64) -> string {
    next: string <- sr_old_step(nodes, root, old);
    case rounds <= 0 or length_bytes(next) == length_bytes(old) of {
        true -> next;
        false -> sr_old_closure(nodes, root, next, rounds - 1)
    }
}

fn sr_has_prim(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], i: int64, n: int64, prim: string) -> boolean {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> false;
        false -> {
            e: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, i);
            case e.kind == 6 and e.name == prim of {
                true -> true;
                false -> sr_has_prim(nodes, i + 1, n, prim)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The value of the let that binds `name` (its node index), or -1.
fn sr_find_let_value(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], i: int64, n: int64, name: string) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> -1;
        false -> {
            e: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, i);
            case e.kind == 2 and (e.name == name or concat("%", e.name) == name or e.name == concat("%", name)) of {
                true -> e.inner;
                false -> sr_find_let_value(nodes, i + 1, n, name)
            }
        }
    }
}

// The subtree at root holds the node target (every child of a node is its inner or its right_expr).
fn sr_contains(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], root: int64, target: int64, depth: int64) -> boolean {
    case root < 0 or target < 0 or depth > 1024 of {
        true -> false;
        false -> case root == target of {
            true -> true;
            false -> {
                n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, root);
                sr_contains(nodes, n.inner, target, depth + 1) or sr_contains(nodes, n.right_expr, target, depth + 1)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_let_binds(let_name: string, name: string) -> boolean {
    let_name == name or concat("%", let_name) == name or let_name == concat("%", name)
}

// The innermost let named `name` whose body holds the node `site` (its index), or best when none does:
// the binding a reference at `site` means. One name can have several lets (every tuple decomposition
// names its root %_td_0), and a let inside another's body is the nearer one.
fn sr_find_let_scoped(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], i: int64, n: int64, name: string, site: int64, best: int64) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> best;
        false -> {
            e: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, i);
            here: boolean <- e.kind == 2 and sr_let_binds(e.name, name) and sr_contains(nodes, e.right_expr, site, 0);
            nearer: boolean <- case here of {
                false -> false;
                true -> case best < 0 of {
                    true -> true;
                    false -> {
                        b: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, best);
                        sr_contains(nodes, b.right_expr, i, 0)
                    }
                }
            };
            next_best: int64 <- case nearer of {
                true -> i;
                false -> best
            };
            sr_find_let_scoped(nodes, i + 1, n, name, site, next_best)
        }
    }
}

// The value (its node index) of the let a reference at `site` to `name` means: the innermost let of the
// name around the reference; when no let of the name holds it, the first let of the name; else -1.
fn sr_find_let_value_at(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], name: string, site: int64) -> int64 {
    n: int64 <- sr_nodes_len(nodes);
    best: int64 <- sr_find_let_scoped(nodes, 0, n, name, site, -1);
    case best < 0 of {
        true -> sr_find_let_value(nodes, 0, n, name);
        false -> {
            b: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, best);
            b.inner
        }
    }
}

// The name at the root of a projection chain, with a decomposition temporary (%_td_N) followed to the
// value it decomposes and a user call named by its function: what W2300 prints for a part kept without
// an update. "?" for a shape not followed.
fn sr_proj_root(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 32 of {
        true -> "?";
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind == 1 of {
                true -> case sr_starts_with(a.name, "%_td_") of {
                    false -> a.name;
                    true -> {
                        v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, a.name, idx);
                        sr_proj_root(nodes, v, depth + 1)
                    }
                };
                false -> case a.kind == 6 and (a.name == "record_proj" or a.name == "tuple_proj") of {
                    true -> sr_proj_root(nodes, a.inner, depth + 1);
                    false -> case a.kind == 4 or a.kind == 5 of {
                        true -> a.name;
                        false -> "?"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ---- the new state -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The result positions of the body, through lets and case arms, to the state element of each result
// tuple. "" when every one is proven; else the first reason.
fn sr_check_result(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, reply_form: boolean, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 64 of {
        true -> "the result shape is not analysed";
        false -> {
            n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case n.kind of {
                2 -> sr_check_result(nodes, n.right_expr, reply_form, old, depth + 1);
                3 -> sr_check_result_arms(nodes, n.right_expr, reply_form, old, depth + 1);
                1 -> {
                    v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, n.name, idx);
                    case v < 0 of {
                        true -> concat("the result is '", concat(n.name, "', whose value is not analysed"));
                        false -> sr_check_result(nodes, v, reply_form, old, depth + 1)
                    }
                };
                4 -> concat("'", concat(n.name, "' is not a logging updater"));
                5 -> concat("'", concat(n.name, "' is not a logging updater"));
                6 -> case n.name == "tuple_make" of {
                    false -> "the result shape is not analysed";
                    true -> case reply_form of {
                        false -> sr_check_state(nodes, n.right_expr, old, depth + 1);
                        true -> {
                            rest: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, n.right_expr);
                            case rest.kind == 6 and rest.name == "tuple_make" of {
                                true -> sr_check_state(nodes, rest.right_expr, old, depth + 1);
                                false -> "the result shape is not analysed"
                            }
                        }
                    }
                };
                _: int64 -> "the result shape is not analysed"
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_check_result_arms(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, reply_form: boolean, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind of {
                7 -> {
                    r: string <- sr_check_result_arms(nodes, a.inner, reply_form, old, depth);
                    case length_bytes(r) > 0 of {
                        true -> r;
                        false -> sr_check_result_arms(nodes, a.right_expr, reply_form, old, depth)
                    }
                };
                8 -> sr_check_result(nodes, a.right_expr, reply_form, old, depth);
                _: int64 -> "the result shape is not analysed"
            }
        }
    }
}

// The new state: an Old projection, or an aggregate whose pointer-carrying operands are each an Old
// projection, kept once.
fn sr_check_state(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    n0: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
    case sr_is_old_proj(nodes, idx, old) or (idx >= 0 and (sr_buffer_operand_ok(n0, old) or sr_literal_operand_ok(n0, old))) of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            r: string <- sr_check_operands(nodes, idx, old, depth);
            case length_bytes(r) > 0 of {
                true -> r;
                false -> sr_first_overlap(sr_state_keys(nodes, idx, old, depth, ","))
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_check_operands(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 64 of {
        true -> "the new state is not analysed";
        false -> {
            n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case n.kind of {
                1 -> {
                    v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, n.name, idx);
                    case v < 0 of {
                        true -> concat("the new state is '", concat(n.name, "', whose value is not analysed"));
                        false -> sr_check_state(nodes, v, old, depth + 1)
                    }
                };
                // Under the tuple buffer shape the new state may be a let chain or a case: each arm's
                // value is checked as a new state of its own (as sr_check_result follows result arms).
                2 -> case sr_in_set(old, "#tuplebuf") of {
                    true -> sr_check_state(nodes, n.right_expr, old, depth + 1);
                    false -> "the new state is not analysed"
                };
                3 -> case sr_in_set(old, "#tuplebuf") of {
                    true -> sr_check_state_arms(nodes, n.right_expr, old, depth + 1);
                    false -> "the new state is not analysed"
                };
                4 -> concat("'", concat(n.name, "' is not a logging updater"));
                5 -> concat("'", concat(n.name, "' is not a logging updater"));
                6 -> case n.name == "record_make" of {
                    true -> sr_check_record_fields(nodes, idx, old, depth);
                    false -> case n.name == "tuple_make" of {
                        true -> {
                            r: string <- sr_check_operand(nodes, n.inner, "0", old, depth);
                            case length_bytes(r) > 0 of {
                                true -> r;
                                false -> sr_check_operand(nodes, n.right_expr, "1", old, depth)
                            }
                        };
                        false -> concat("the new state is built by '", concat(n.name, "', which is not analysed"))
                    }
                };
                _: int64 -> "the new state is not analysed"
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_check_state_arms(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> case depth > 64 of {
            true -> "the new state is not analysed";
            false -> {
                a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
                case a.kind of {
                    7 -> {
                        r: string <- sr_check_state_arms(nodes, a.inner, old, depth + 1);
                        case length_bytes(r) > 0 of {
                            true -> r;
                            false -> sr_check_state_arms(nodes, a.right_expr, old, depth + 1)
                        }
                    };
                    8 -> sr_check_state(nodes, a.right_expr, old, depth + 1);
                    _: int64 -> "the new state is not analysed"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_check_record_fields(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            f: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case f.kind == 6 and f.name == "record_make" of {
                false -> "";
                true -> {
                    r: string <- sr_check_operand(nodes, f.inner, f.value, old, depth);
                    case length_bytes(r) > 0 of {
                        true -> r;
                        false -> sr_check_record_fields(nodes, f.right_expr, old, depth)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// One operand of the new state's aggregate: a scalar is anything; a pointer-carrying operand is an Old
// projection or a nested aggregate of such.
fn sr_check_operand(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, slot: string, old: string, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            o: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case sr_type_may_point(o.type_name) == false or sr_buffer_operand_ok(o, old) of {
                true -> "";
                false -> case sr_is_old_proj(nodes, idx, old) of {
                    true -> "";
                    false -> case o.kind == 6 and (o.name == "record_make" or o.name == "tuple_make") of {
                        true -> sr_check_state(nodes, idx, old, depth + 1);
                        false -> case o.kind == 4 or o.kind == 5 of {
                            true -> concat("'", concat(o.name, "' is not a logging updater"));
                            false -> case o.kind == 1 of {
                                true -> {
                                    v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, o.name, idx);
                                    case v < 0 of {
                                        true -> concat("slot '", concat(slot, concat("' is replaced without an update (by '", concat(o.name, "')"))));
                                        false -> sr_check_operand(nodes, v, slot, old, depth + 1)
                                    }
                                };
                                false -> case o.kind == 6 and (o.name == "record_proj" or o.name == "tuple_proj") of {
                                    true -> {
                                        root_name: string <- sr_proj_root(nodes, idx, 0);
                                        concat("slot '", concat(slot, concat("' is replaced without an update (by a part of '", concat(root_name, "')"))))
                                    };
                                    false -> concat("slot '", concat(slot, "' is replaced without an update"))
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The projection keys of the pointer-carrying operands kept in the new state (with repeats).
fn sr_state_keys(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, old: string, depth: int64, acc: string) -> string {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 64 of {
        true -> acc;
        false -> {
            n: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case sr_type_may_point(n.type_name) == false of {
                true -> acc;
                false -> case sr_is_old_proj(nodes, idx, old) of {
                    true -> concat(acc, concat(sr_norm_key(nodes, idx, 0), ","));
                    false -> case n.kind == 1 of {
                        true -> {
                            v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, n.name, idx);
                            case v < 0 of { true -> acc; false -> sr_state_keys(nodes, v, old, depth + 1, acc) }
                        };
                        false -> case n.kind == 6 and n.name == "record_make" of {
                            true -> sr_state_keys(nodes, n.right_expr, old, depth, sr_state_keys(nodes, n.inner, old, depth + 1, acc));
                            false -> case n.kind == 6 and n.name == "tuple_make" of {
                                true -> sr_state_keys(nodes, n.right_expr, old, depth + 1, sr_state_keys(nodes, n.inner, old, depth + 1, acc));
                                false -> acc
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// All state buffers (Lee 2026-11-01, design §4.2): a proven behaviour must keep every old node a buffer
// can hide in, because nothing but the fallback copy frees a buffer outside the buffer shapes. Under
// P2 with keys that are disjoint positions of the old state, the kept operands of a same-typed new
// state cover every old position (each new position takes one old position of its type, injectively,
// without nesting), so no old buffer is dropped. Two spellings of one position (`s.p` for a bind arm
// `s` over the state, `x` for `x <- state.p`) and a position kept beside one inside it (`state.p` and
// `state.p.x`) broke that: the keys are therefore normalised to the parameter's spelling, and a key
// that is a prefix of another counts as kept twice.

// The scrutinee of the case one of whose `bind` arms binds name, or -1.
fn sr_bind_scrutinee(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], i: int64, n: int64, name: string) -> int64 {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> -1;
        false -> {
            e: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, i);
            case e.kind == 3 and sr_arms_bind(nodes, e.right_expr, name, 0) of {
                true -> e.inner;
                false -> sr_bind_scrutinee(nodes, i + 1, n, name)
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_arms_bind(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, name: string, depth: int64) -> boolean {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 256 of {
        true -> false;
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind of {
                7 -> sr_arms_bind(nodes, a.inner, name, depth + 1) or sr_arms_bind(nodes, a.right_expr, name, depth + 1);
                8 -> a.value == "bind" and (a.name == name or concat("%", a.name) == name or a.name == concat("%", name));
                _: int64 -> false
            }
        }
    }
}

fn sr_strip_pct(name: string) -> string {
    case sr_starts_with(name, "%") of {
        true -> substring(name, 1, length_bytes(name));
        false -> name
    }
}

// The key of an Old name referenced at node `site`: the key of the projection the let in scope binds it
// to, else of the scrutinee a bind arm binds it to, else the name itself (the parameter).
fn sr_norm_root(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], name: string, site: int64, depth: int64) -> string {
    case depth > 16 of {
        true -> "?";
        false -> {
            v: int64 <- sr_find_let_value_at(nodes, name, site);
            case v >= 0 of {
                true -> sr_norm_key(nodes, v, depth + 1);
                false -> {
                    s: int64 <- sr_bind_scrutinee(nodes, 0, sr_nodes_len(nodes), name);
                    case s >= 0 of {
                        true -> sr_norm_key(nodes, s, depth + 1);
                        false -> sr_strip_pct(name)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The projection's path for the one-slot rule (P2), "state.items" / "state.0", with every Old name
// replaced by its normalised key; "?" for a shape not followed.
fn sr_norm_key(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], idx: int64, depth: int64) -> string {
    case idx < 0 or depth > 16 of {
        true -> "?";
        false -> {
            a: { kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 } <- sr_node_at(nodes, idx);
            case a.kind == 1 of {
                true -> sr_norm_root(nodes, a.name, idx, depth);
                false -> case a.kind == 6 and a.name == "record_proj" of {
                    true -> concat(sr_norm_key(nodes, a.inner, depth + 1), concat(".", a.value));
                    false -> case a.kind == 6 and a.name == "tuple_proj" of {
                        true -> concat(sr_norm_key(nodes, a.inner, depth + 1), concat(".", sr_node_at(nodes, a.right_expr).value));
                        false -> "?"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// k and k2 name the same position or one inside the other.
fn sr_keys_overlap(k: string, k2: string) -> boolean {
    k == k2 or sr_starts_with(k2, concat(k, ".")) or sr_starts_with(k, concat(k2, ".")) or k == "?" or k2 == "?"
}

// The first key of keys (",a,b,") that overlaps k, or "".
fn sr_overlap_in(keys: string, k: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(keys) <= 1 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            rest: string <- substring(keys, 1, length_bytes(keys));
            e: int64 <- sr_find_from(rest, ",", 0);
            case e < 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> {
                    k2: string <- substring(rest, 0, e);
                    case sr_keys_overlap(k, k2) of {
                        true -> k2;
                        false -> sr_overlap_in(substring(rest, e, length_bytes(rest)), k)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// ",a,b,a," (or a key inside another): "version 'k' is kept twice in the new state" (W2300's existing reason).
fn sr_first_overlap(keys: string) -> string {
    case length_bytes(keys) <= 1 of {
        true -> "";
        false -> {
            rest: string <- substring(keys, 1, length_bytes(keys));
            e: int64 <- sr_find_from(rest, ",", 0);
            case e < 0 of {
                true -> "";
                false -> {
                    k: string <- substring(rest, 0, e);
                    tail: string <- substring(rest, e, length_bytes(rest));
                    case length_bytes(sr_overlap_in(tail, k)) > 0 of {
                        true -> concat("version '", concat(k, "' is kept twice in the new state"));
                        false -> sr_first_overlap(tail)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// "" when the behaviour is proven (or the function is no behaviour); else the reason W2300 prints.
fn behaviour_release_reason(fn_val: { name: string, return_type: string, effects: string, body: { nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], root: int64 }, param_names: string, param_types: string }) -> string {
    rt: string <- sr_strip_spaces(fn_val.return_type);
    case sr_starts_with(rt, "(:reply,") or sr_starts_with(rt, "(:no_reply,") of {
        false -> "";
        true -> {
            pname: string <- sr_param_at(fn_val.param_names, 1);
            case length_bytes(pname) == 0 of {
                true -> "the behaviour has no state parameter";
                false -> case sr_type_may_point(sr_state_type(rt)) == false of {
                    true -> "";
                    false -> {
                        // The buffer shapes of §4.2 (state_buffer_variant) mark the Old set: "#bufstate"
                        // accepts buffer-valued operands, "#litstate" an atom literal new state. No SIR
                        // name starts with '#'.
                        variant: string <- state_buffer_variant(rt);
                        old0: string <- case sr_region_buffer_tuple(rt) of {
                            true -> sr_add(sr_add(sr_add_both(",", pname), "#bufstate"), "#tuplebuf");
                            false -> case length_bytes(variant) == 0 of {
                                true -> sr_add_both(",", pname);
                                false -> case sr_literal_state_ok(rt, variant) of {
                                    true -> sr_add(sr_add(sr_add_both(",", pname), "#bufstate"), "#litstate");
                                    false -> sr_add(sr_add_both(",", pname), "#bufstate")
                                }
                            }
                        };
                        closed: string <- sr_old_closure(fn_val.body.nodes, fn_val.body.root, old0, 8);
                        old: string <- sr_strip_marked(closed, 0, ",");
                        case sr_in_set(old, "!") of {
                            true -> concat("a pattern on '", concat(pname, "' hides its parts"));
                            false -> case sr_has_prim(fn_val.body.nodes, 0, sr_nodes_len(fn_val.body.nodes), "write_ref") of {
                                true -> "write_ref during the dispatch may store a frame value into an old state cell";
                                false -> sr_check_result(fn_val.body.nodes, fn_val.body.root, sr_starts_with(rt, "(:reply,"), old, 0)
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// A SIR node named `name`, of any kind, at index i or later.
fn sr_has_name(nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], i: int64, n: int64, name: string) -> boolean {
    case i >= n of {
        true -> false;
        false -> case sr_node_at(nodes, i).name == name of {
            true -> true;
            false -> sr_has_name(nodes, i + 1, n, name)
        }
    }
}

// The pin rule (chunk15_stack_memory_design.md §7, Lee 2026-11-01): a behaviour that allocates a buffer C
// keeps (alloc_buf_retained) holds it as a node of its state area, which must never move. "" when the
// function allocates no such buffer; else "E4037:<reason>" when its state release is not proven (the
// fallback copy, §4.4, would move the buffer), or "E4039:" when it calls compact_state() (§4.7). The
// pipeline reports these as errors instead of W2300.
fn behaviour_pin_error(fn_val: { name: string, return_type: string, effects: string, body: { nodes: List[{ kind: int64, type_name: string, value: string, name: string, inner: int64, right_expr: int64 }, mem(normal)], root: int64 }, param_names: string, param_types: string }) -> string {
    n: int64 <- sr_nodes_len(fn_val.body.nodes);
    case sr_has_name(fn_val.body.nodes, 0, n, "alloc_buf_retained") of {
        false -> "";
        true -> case sr_has_name(fn_val.body.nodes, 0, n, "compact_state") of {
            true -> "E4039:";
            false -> {
                reason: string <- behaviour_release_reason(fn_val);
                case length_bytes(reason) > 0 of {
                    true -> concat("E4037:", reason);
                    false -> ""
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
